# Golden: Phase-7 node 9210 (Option-2 generated lead) -- "ballad" style, VarD
# peak section, a |C|F| two-bar change. Locks ballad's generated kLeadMotif
# (the new TrackRole::kLead pattern in ballad.hpp's kVarDPatterns, no other
# section) -- the reflection's own most-conspicuous model gap, "a ballad style
# with no vocal-style line at all": seed=1503, length=3, center_degree=2 (the
# 3rd, the classic vocal-melody color tone), vel=62, gate=kGateHeld (3600
# ticks -- each onset's tail overlaps the next by design, a single continuous
# legato line rather than three separate stabs), idiom_role=kDrums (onset
# candidates drawn from kVarDDrums' own 8-step even-16th kick/snare/ride
# mask), gm_program=53 (Voice Oohs -- the literal "vocal-style" line, owner
# sign-off, see docs/proposals/phase7-9210-motif-generate-option2-leads.md
# section 4.3). Note ballad's OWN existing golden (arranger_voicing.acmd) only
# exercises varA -- varD (and this kLead line) has zero prior coverage. Two
# full bars of VarD exercise BOTH halves of the call-and-response repeat
# policy (motif.hpp's apply_repeat): bar 1 (repeat=0, over C) plays the
# generated phrase verbatim -- the "statement" -- and bar 2 (repeat=1, over F)
# applies the seed's own kDiatonicTranspose with a repeat-keyed amount -- the
# "answer". Routes drums/bass/chord1 following arranger_band.acmd's own
# convention, plus `style route lead synth:7` -- WITHOUT this route the new
# kLead content never appears in the golden at all (the gap this fixture
# closes). Any accidental change to ballad's kLeadMotif or to kVarDDrums'
# onset mask moves these notes/ticks and fails this test.
key C major
port open out virt as synth
chord out synth:4
style load ballad
style route drums synth:10
style route bass synth:2
style route chord1 synth:3
style route lead synth:7
style section varD
seq new verse
seq add C 1bar
seq add F 1bar
seq loop on
seq play
transport start
advance 7680
quit
